lling picard that it's over between  them deanna figures out what her mother  is doing and tells picard he will have  to fight for her in a display so  melodramatic it would even make william  shatner groan picard professes his love  for luaxana threatens tog with  annihilation and recites famous lines  from shakespearean sonnets with as much  grandiose flair as he can muster  my  love is a fever  longing still for that which longer  nurses the disease  worf watches in disgust looking like  he's about to rage puke it's picard like  you've never seen him and probably  wouldn't want to see him again  in star trek the original series the  season 2 episode the trouble with  tribble starts off on a serious note the  enterprise is already on its way to deep  space station k7 but they put the pedal  to the metal when they receive an alert  that their destination is under attack  this alert proves to be a false alarm  though dangers do await at k7 a  domineering federation bureaucrat a  klingon spy and a space trader named  cyrano jones who sells members of the  enterprise crew some of the most  troublesome pets in the galaxy tribbles  the trouble with tribbles is a classic  and one of the first examples of a  whimsically goofy original series  episode that makes a point of not taking  itself too seriously from the countless  puffballs that multiply faster than a  gremlin in a tropical storm to the  ridiculous bar room brawl between the  klingons and enterprise crew to the  peddler cyrano jones willing to risk  life and limb in order to score a free  drink the trouble with tribbles is a  great time  to celebrate his upcoming marriage to  dad zia in the ds9 episode titled you  are cordially invited dwarf invites  chief o'brien and dr bashir among others  to the ritual of kalhaya thinking they  can expect the klingon version of a  bachelor party they happily accept but  rather than drinking or exotic dancers  the path to kauhai involves fasting for  four days and nights being drained of  blood hanging from a pole over intense  heat and other creative forms of torture  when wharf abruptly cancels the wedding  bashir and o'brien are thrilled to cut  their torment short  they head straight to quarks for a feast  but before they can sink their teeth in  cisco and martok arrive to let them know  the wedding's back on when quark takes  their untouched food away you can  practically hear them whining like  disappointed puppies  after several vowels from both friends  that they're going to kill wharf the  wedding finally arrives part of the  friend's duty as per klingon tradition  is to attack wharf and jazia with  blunted weapons called mastakas while  everyone else applauds the newlyweds  kiss bashir looks like obi-wan kenobi  waiting for a force field to come down  now  not yet  martok finally gives the word bashir and  o'brien rush wharf and jadzia with cries  of rage and the credits roll to sounds  of the mock battle  one of the best star trek films  featuring the original cast is 1986's  star trek iv the voyage home in order to  answer an alien probe's call which is  blindly triggering power losses and  apocalyptic storms on earth kirk and his  crew must go back in time to recover a  humpback whale a species extinct by the  23rd century while original series sent  the heroes back in time on multiple  occasions none of those stories feel as  natural or believable as in star trek iv  rather than experiencing any particular  physical threat the biggest challenge  they face is culture shock they don't  have money when they try to use a bus  they're foiled by the need for exact  change and in particular they're  confused by what spock calls quote  colorful metaphors i.e all the swearing  the best scene involves kirk and spock  trying to earn the trust of the marine  biologist dr jillian taylor kirk is  attempting and failing to seem like the  normal one compared to spock when kirk  suggests the three of them get dinner  one of the most natural adorably funny  moments in the franchise unfolds you  guys like italian  no no no yes  no yes  i love italian  due to the meddling of the mischievous  entity q one of star trek's greatest  villains captain picard his senior staff  and picard's old flame vosh find  themselves transported to sherwood  forest in season 4's cupid there's  little about cupid that won't make you  laugh picard and his senior officers are  made up as robin hood's merry men  including data who bears the famous bald  dome of friar tuck wharf is predictably  the most incensed by the situation  famously complaining to picard sir  i protest i am not a merry man  the most laugh out loud moment comes as  jordy rests and plucks at his mandolin  without comment or permission worf  calmly walks over grabs the instrument  and smashes it against a nearby tree  the prime directive prohibits members of  starfleet from interfering with the  natural progression of any society  outside the united federation of planets  serving as a comically dangerous example  of why this code exists is the original  series season 2 episode a piece of the  action 100 years before the events of  the episode sigma eosha 2 is visited by  the earthship horizon  to help teach the planet's natives the  horizon crew leaves behind a number of  books including a non-fiction book  titled chicago mobs of the 20s after the  horizon leaves the eoceans come to see  this book as a holy text and base their  entire culture on it when kirk spock and  mccoy beam down to the planet they find  a world where just about every grown  male dresses and speaks like tough guys  in mobster movies people openly carry  tommy guns up and down the street as if  there's nothing strange about it a piece  of the action gets even funnier once  kirk and spock are outfitted in their  own mobster getups and kirk attempts a  chicago gangster impersonation shatner  wouldn't fool anyone on earth and it's  tough to tell whether that's intentional  which just makes t